 Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.
   The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).
   Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

   Task 1: Remove old Docker versions.
   Description Task 1: This task is responsible for ensuring that any old or obsolete versions of Docker are not present on the system. It uses the 'package' module to remove the packages listed in the 'docker_obsolete_packages' variable.

   Task 2: Add Docker GPG key.
   Description Task 2: This task adds the Docker GPG key to the system. The key is specified using the 'docker_yum_gpg_key' variable. The task only runs if the 'docker_add_repo' variable is set to true.

   Task 3: Add Docker repository.
   Description Task 3: This task adds the Docker repository to the system. The repository URL is specified using the 'docker_yum_repo_url' variable. The task only runs if the 'docker_add_repo' variable is set to true.

   Task 4: Configure Docker Nightly repo.
   Description Task 4: This task configures the Docker Nightly repository on the system. It uses the 'ini_file' module to set the 'enabled' option in the appropriate section of the Docker repository configuration file. The value for the 'enabled' option is specified using the 'docker_yum_repo_enable_nightly' variable. The task only runs if the 'docker_add_repo' variable is set to true.

   Task 5: Configure Docker Test repo.
   Description Task 5: This task configures the Docker Test repository on the system. It uses the 'ini_file' module to set the 'enabled' option in the appropriate section of the Docker repository configuration file. The value for the 'enabled' option is specified using the 'docker_yum_repo_enable_test' variable. The task only runs if the 'docker_add_repo' variable is set to true.

   Task 6: Configure containerd on RHEL 8.
   Description Task 6: This task configures containerd on RHEL 8 systems. It removes the 'runc' package and installs the 'container-selinux' and 'containerd.io' packages. The task only runs if the system is running RHEL 8.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Remove old Docker versions
  package:
    name: "{{ docker_obsolete_packages }}"
    state: absent

- name: Add Docker GPG key
  apt_key:
    url: "{{ docker_yum_gpg_key }}"
    state: present
  when: docker_add_repo is bool

- name: Add Docker repository
  yum_repository:
    name: docker
    description: Docker Repository
    baseurl: "{{ docker_yum_repo_url }}"
    enabled: yes
    gpgcheck: yes
    gpgkey: "{{ docker_yum_gpg_key }}"
  when: docker_add_repo is bool

- name: Configure Docker Nightly repo
  ini_file:
    dest: /etc/yum.repos.d/docker.repo
    section: docker-{{ docker_yum_repo_nightly_name }}
    option: enabled
    value: "{{ docker_yum_repo_enable_nightly|default('0') }}"
  when: docker_add_repo is bool

- name: Configure Docker Test repo
  ini_file:
    dest: /etc/yum.repos.d/docker.repo
    section: docker-{{ docker_yum_repo_test_name }}
    option: enabled
    value: "{{ docker_yum_repo_enable_test|default('0') }}"
  when: docker_add_repo is bool

- name: Configure containerd on RHEL 8
  block:
    - name: Remove runc package
      package:
        name: runc
        state: absent
    - name: Install container-selinux package
      package:
        name: container-selinux
        state: present
    - name: Install containerd.io package
      package:
        name: containerd.io
        state: present
  when: ansible_distribution == 'RedHat' and ansible_distribution_major_version == '8'

